  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LB-Municipal Dev. &amp; Finance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Proposed project was to be a follow-up on First Municipal Infrastructure Project, but added the municipal policy development aspect to the 1st project was had focussed on uprgading municipal physical infrastructure. A PHRD-funded preparation facility was to assess the policy context and make recommendations in terms of fiscal decentralization, potential for market-based financing of local infrastructure, address budgeting for and pricing of local services, and institutional framework for service provision, etc... The government agencies which are counterpart to this effort (including ministry of Interior) lacked the commitment to address these important policy dimensions and were mainly interested in a project that would have been weak in terms of -- if not fully devoid of -- policy reforms. The proposed project was therefore dropped from the pipeline.</narrative>
  </description>
